{"title":"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Ceva)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Ceva)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Thorough_&amp;_Has_diagram)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Thorough &amp; Has diagram)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">Triangle</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Isosceles_triangle\" title=\"Isosceles triangle\"> isosceles</a> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/9/f99228fedde4b9ee40f739fa50129f9c98962aec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = BC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/426318b24f4c1895269172812bd61e252b1c44cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB = 106^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"118\" height=\"13\" /> Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is in the interior of the triangle so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/0/2c0e17c90e2dca44bf815d6db3b83fcef6072b9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MAC = 7^\\circ$\" width=\"99\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/1/df108fb91b6df8c2d55deb9933ace7fe0010e9d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MCA = 23^\\circ.$\" width=\"114\" height=\"13\" /> Find the number of degrees in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/f/2ff54a430b8e3091dc7de42e4b9df1886fbc2ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CMB.$\" width=\"65\" height=\"12\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec8d127e80906c0e7baf73d163450eef066397cc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pointpen = black; pathpen = black+linewidth(0.7); size(220);  /* We will WLOG AB = 2 to draw following */  pair A=(0,0), B=(2,0), C=(1,Tan(37)), M=IP(A--(2Cos(30),2Sin(30)),B--B+(-2,2Tan(23))), N=(2-M.x,M.y);  D(MP(&quot;A&quot;,A)--MP(&quot;B&quot;,B)--MP(&quot;C&quot;,C,N)--cycle); D(A--D(MP(&quot;M&quot;,M))--B); D(C--M); D(C--D(MP(&quot;N&quot;,N))--B--N--M,linetype(&quot;6 6&quot;)+linewidth(0.7));  [/asy]\" width=\"368\" height=\"168\" /></center>\n<p>Take point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/1/aa1255d03a67ad70490f8d209a38d37bec8a146c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CBN = 7^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/4/f849e44371b0f68d934d48398e6bc68c11789116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCN = 23^\\circ$\" width=\"106\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/6/2f638e3a912fbd5eccd3e81d971058f50dd9b6d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MCN = 106^\\circ - 2\\cdot 23^\\circ = 60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"241\" height=\"13\" />. Also, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/3431b35dcd263cac56e5c8a8aed399ba0ce6fce2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AMC$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/e/0fe5c17329fb93f96ffaefdadbdd81658aefe534.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BNC$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> are congruent (by ASA), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/0/660eadea71a736658d726a69b0798c8c39031ab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CM = CN$\" width=\"89\" height=\"12\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/0/730b40fde1b9321a16de1ec53fdc592ce98cb61b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CMN$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equilateral_triangle\" title=\"Equilateral triangle\">equilateral triangle</a>, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb33aa203c19f2ded5071a74215487f3458b3f03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CNM = 60^\\circ$\" width=\"111\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/f/a8fa87967836020c02d19f7daf67d241ca1e3903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MNB = 360^\\circ - \\angle CNM - \\angle CNB = 360^\\circ - 60^\\circ - 150^\\circ = 150^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"514\" height=\"16\" />. We now see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/1/221a2cd89904fddc1f89bef10e60dbe283aa5666.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle MNB$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/4/814ac219af4c1f8055a4d64435fbec0748946036.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CNB$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> are congruent. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/a/6cae3fb85a9e6867457736e90ff961ac4f545474.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB = MB$\" width=\"87\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/7/8d7acb72f07ba3a58bf7e922cb9af230b8686d0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CMB = \\angle MCB = \\boxed{83^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"209\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the givens, we have the following <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle\" title=\"Angle\">angle</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Measure\" title=\"Measure\">measures</a>: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/1/b61f394019c2c78b8c2bc2c741a9ef8688f7060d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle AMC = 150^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"133\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/4/304f4154ce88ce070e311dea03c5a39f1a755d11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle MCB = 83^\\circ$\" width=\"125\" height=\"13\" />.  If we define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/5/5354503401b46cf7a79403b513a61c21c883c031.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle CMB = \\theta$\" width=\"110\" height=\"13\" /> then we also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc6dc42bb5dc44dfc781b09d406409e497260b9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle CBM = 97^\\circ - \\theta$\" width=\"158\" height=\"13\" />.  Then apply the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Sines\" title=\"Law of Sines\">Law of Sines</a> to triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/3431b35dcd263cac56e5c8a8aed399ba0ce6fce2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AMC$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/a/0faed260933ee64e9300b5750492d63184fc7687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BMC$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" /> to get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/a/0ba2b582bcb8aca8d0fcbca0e142e071352eb30f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sin 150^\\circ}{\\sin 7^\\circ} = \\frac{AC}{CM} = \\frac{BC}{CM} = \\frac{\\sin \\theta}{\\sin (97^\\circ - \\theta)}\\]\" width=\"306\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>Clearing <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Denominator\" title=\"Denominator\">denominators</a>, evaluating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/4/7c49daa29a0086b9c28e12ad174fc6fbcc1ba99c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin 150^\\circ = \\frac 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"96\" height=\"37\" /> and applying one of our <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trigonometric_identities\" title=\"Trigonometric identities\">trigonometric identities</a> to the result gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/c/89c211497b262b45d3aeb2a00921f315194b202f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2} \\cos (7^\\circ - \\theta )= \\sin 7^\\circ \\sin \\theta\\]\" width=\"203\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>and multiplying through by 2 and applying the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/Trigonometric_identities#Double-angle_identities%7C\">double angle formulas</a> gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/f/aef237179cb2c6f4f96e5c906ab00cf00cdf20a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos 7^\\circ\\cos\\theta + \\sin7^\\circ\\sin\\theta = 2 \\sin7^\\circ \\sin\\theta\\]\" width=\"300\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/9/54959ab097d87bad6fc8619be7384a39262fa1d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 7^\\circ \\cos \\theta = \\sin 7^\\circ \\sin\\theta \\Longleftrightarrow \\tan 7^{\\circ} = \\cot \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"336\" height=\"13\" />; since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/2/a12c8cdfce7133f5fef523411a812812cf2ae3c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^\\circ &lt; \\theta &lt; 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/f/a6f99e5db68bc54dd691537297e22255dafa4ac0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = 83^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/b/2cb8f0f68df3e2a50968e2b3b575a6aa4af3a3c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{83}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Without_loss_of_generality\" title=\"Without loss of generality\">Without loss of generality</a>, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/e/b9e2e39dbe93c8b95605112ba63c466a92e6286e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = BC = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"113\" height=\"13\" />.  Then, using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Sines\" title=\"Law of Sines\">Law of Sines</a> in triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/01927bf7bbcf5688067a91087d440c77879049b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AMC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50a8de7bac8e2c8e6e7b1c3f5c39127f3c5ae849.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {1}{\\sin 150} = \\frac {MC}{\\sin 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"117\" height=\"38\" />, and using the sine addition formula to evaluate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ac066e89da9d77022a167fec14aab4e938acfca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin 150 = \\sin (90 + 60)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"170\" height=\"18\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f68c294dd25b59d72807f53b24ffd9f503f9346.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MC = 2 \\sin 7$\" width=\"104\" height=\"12\" />.  \n</p><p>Then, using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a> in triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/673d4b51ddc68d677812d71b9ecb0f739e31f1a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MCB$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/5/ef5b6fab22dbae350ed04261591bf4787b98fda1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MB^2 = 4\\sin^2 7 + 1 - 4\\sin 7(\\cos 83) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"312\" height=\"20\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/a/03a9e8c5f2815e2973443d0765b874d3b5c09b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 83 = \\sin 7$\" width=\"104\" height=\"12\" />. So triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/673d4b51ddc68d677812d71b9ecb0f739e31f1a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MCB$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> is isosceles, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0deb2ccb8b6037e09a8fbad17eef90d1c32977b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CMB = \\boxed{83}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note: A diagram would be much appreciated; I cannot make one since I'm bad at asymptote. Also, please make this less cluttered&#160;:) ~tauros\n</p><p>First, take point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> outside of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/6/22613adb57fa8713be9af69b430c14e0b2247624.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{CEB}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is equilateral. Then, connect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Also, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a30c9c946a561bfb130894432aa55948d58b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/4/7141050209eac2fad78faac18eec87f7490883d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{MCE} = 83^\\circ - 60^\\circ = 23^\\circ$\" width=\"207\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/9/bf9fceb3e36db1476bad7e9edcf77e25a3ee00a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE = AB$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, and (trivially) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/c/9ccbf0d246994f37c5521128aa5455dff4a1652a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CM = CM$\" width=\"91\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4a98700298838eb36fbe65035e9af775a736f63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{MCE} \\cong  \\triangle{MCA}$\" width=\"152\" height=\"13\" /> by SAS congruence. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/7886b6e66266e2ca83892466637d9ec7427ce7cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CMA} = \\angle{CME} = 150^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"203\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02f3cf425ce682bf50fcd3269249be8ae25a4068.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{AME} = 60^\\circ$\" width=\"109\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/d/5fdbe3bb82e1bddca883238394f52748aa2311db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM = ME$\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />,\nmaking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/b/3fbb6633d950213aef23457350ace7d592eddcfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AME}$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> also equilateral. (it is isosceles with a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> angle) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/cce75ea8e481f655039ca61fff18bb360b0b057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{MAF} \\cong \\triangle{EAF}$\" width=\"146\" height=\"13\" /> by SAS (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/8/548c0091406a67605ccd6ed4bb252134ad705244.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MA = AE$\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" />, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/f/a8ff7f0b96ed01f9277cd157588958998b703cc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF = AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94b32bcef4f63a95ab2def300b4ae37ac672c7c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle{MAF} = m\\angle{EAF} = 30^\\circ$\" width=\"220\" height=\"13\" />), and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/f/9afa4fda48df3d0d6bcfbea2cdbe25954ed81a9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{MAB} \\cong \\triangle{EAB}$\" width=\"146\" height=\"13\" /> by SAS (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/8/548c0091406a67605ccd6ed4bb252134ad705244.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MA = AE$\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/9/9b95309f51bafc06e986229bac75aaca001b36ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AB$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, and \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/a/b0ae82d59d7528406a5c0a1440507758385ca3ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle{MAB} = m\\angle{EAB} = 30^\\circ$\" width=\"221\" height=\"13\" />). Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/2/fc200a04d9c8e6c6662f2c5f9c1392402a4aa76c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{BME}$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" /> is isosceles, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/4/6044ef082091d3e2dbf62b4ddc9924b4b5c287a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle{BME} = m\\angle{BEM} = 60^\\circ + 7^\\circ = 67^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"316\" height=\"14\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/f/88ff89f622a0bab0578422027350d10cdd0136ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{EMB} + \\angle {CMB} = \\angle{CME} = 150^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"288\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d74e15fced375dc73df35bd65f08d56477b49b53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CME} = 150^\\circ - 67^\\circ  = \\boxed{83^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"230\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Ceva.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Ceva)\">Solution 5 (Ceva)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Ceva)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Noticing that we have three concurrent cevians, we apply Ceva's theorem:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/3/f23bde86479282affe7a8c21cdd605437c7bb1fd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\sin \\angle ACM)(\\sin \\angle BAM)(\\sin \\angle CBM) = (\\sin \\angle CAM)(\\sin \\angle ABM)(\\sin \\angle BCM)\\]\" width=\"623\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d857b60c72c39859b0a2c60964de88e14b2b228b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\sin 23)(\\sin 30)(\\sin x) = (\\sin 7)(\\sin 37-x)(\\sin 83)\\]\" width=\"382\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>using the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/9/db933d291ddd23a0956688f096e2b74dd1d39d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin 83 = \\cos 7$\" width=\"104\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/9/6f96bf01afb710f5c8320aefe7bc7f2e58e64d04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sin 7)(\\cos 7) = 1/2 (\\sin 14)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"206\" height=\"18\" /> we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/0/b50ed937710c02e0725a948c61a77c7e4b0d5d6f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\sin 23)(\\sin x) = (\\sin 14)(\\sin 37-x)\\]\" width=\"277\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>By inspection, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/e/cfe18293fc6889cc92097ca356007d8f0da6a9f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=14^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> works, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/9147a2dfb6fa0ab2e16cb494f89177749884715b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180-83-14= \\boxed{083}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"171\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/e/0ee9f6a86f7bf36db40c560d8766da8e4364c4d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{APC} = \\theta^{\\circ}$\" width=\"94\" height=\"13\" />\nUsing sine rule on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/3/ee3c085126d6ae9e287189fffcd40f33985f090d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{APB}, \\triangle{APC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"125\" height=\"17\" />, letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/f/16f128c20d9a8acd9a5fd63fa67d118ae846c267.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP=d$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> we get&#160;:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d82346f110e6eb643cd97295d5799a1ca013ea1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{1} = \\frac{\\sin{7^{\\circ}}}{\\sin{150^{\\circ}}} = 2\\sin{7^{\\circ}}= \\frac{\\sin{14^{\\circ}}}{\\cos{7^{\\circ}}}= \\frac{\\sin{14^{\\circ}}}{\\sin{83^{\\circ}}}= \\frac{\\sin{(97-\\theta)^{\\circ}}}{\\sin{\\theta^{\\circ}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"462\" height=\"39\" />\nSimplifying, we get that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8c6e0276b9eda5f7a71f897f4e6234d8e8cff88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{(14-\\theta)^{\\circ}}-\\cos{(14+\\theta)^{\\circ}}=\\cos{(14-\\theta)^{\\circ}}-\\cos{(180-\\theta)^{\\circ}},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"476\" height=\"18\" /> from where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/9/f3979726c687b349269cd9473550dcdc5b913735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{(14-\\theta)^{\\circ}}=\\cos{(180-\\theta)^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"229\" height=\"18\" />\nSimplifying more, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/0/2400fcd474ad59682b4041554b84e0db259db5cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{97^{\\circ}} \\cdot \\sin{(\\theta-83)^{\\circ}} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"193\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/3/be3def498794af8dd98f0f93c17d20c585e33901.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = 83^{\\circ}$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />\nNOTE: The simplifications were carried out by the product-to-sum and sum-to-product identities \n~Prabh1512\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Thorough_.26_Has_diagram.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Thorough_&amp;_Has_diagram)\">Solution 7 (Thorough &amp; Has diagram)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Thorough &amp; Has diagram)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/f/bcfee8d148011a8be7bb8467b12a0c863e982180.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad;  pair C = (0,0); pair A = (1,0); pair B = (Cos(106), Sin(106));   unitsize(10cm);  dot(&quot;C&quot;, C, SW); dot(&quot;A&quot;, A, SE); dot(&quot;B&quot;, B, NW);  draw(A--B--C--cycle);  pair P = ((Cos(106)+1)/2, Sin(106)/2); dot(&quot;P&quot;, P, NE); draw(C--P);  pair M = (0.224362644183, 0.0952362921539); dot(&quot;M&quot;, M, S);  pair M2 = (0.029704273724, 0.2419218955997); dot(&quot;M&#39;&quot;, M2, N);  draw(C--M--M2--cycle); draw(M--A--M2--cycle); draw(M--B--M2--cycle);  // Colors pen redAngle    = red + linewidth(1.2); pen blueAngle   = blue + linewidth(1.2); pen greenAngle  = heavygreen + linewidth(1.2); pen purpleAngle = purple + linewidth(1.2); pen orangeAngle = orange + linewidth(1.2); pen brownAngle  = brown + linewidth(1.2); pen cyanAngle   = deepcyan + linewidth(1.2);  // 7 degrees path ang = anglemark(M, A, C);  draw(ang, redAngle); label(&quot;$7^{\\circ}$&quot;, ang, dir(ang), red);  // 23 degrees path ang2 = anglemark(A, C, M);  draw(ang2, blueAngle); label(&quot;$23^{\\circ}$&quot;, ang2, SE, blue);  // 60 degrees path ang3 = anglemark(M, C, M2);  draw(ang3, greenAngle); label(&quot;$60^{\\circ}$&quot;, ang3, NE, heavygreen);  // theta path ang4 = anglemark(M2, A, M);  draw(ang4, purpleAngle); label(&quot;$\\theta$&quot;, ang4, 2NW, purple);  // 30 - theta path ang5 = anglemark(M, M2, A);  draw(ang5, orangeAngle); label(&quot;$30-\\theta$&quot;, ang5, NE, orange);  [/asy]\" width=\"645\" height=\"495\" />\nConstruct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec86336910461366c64cea3efebada7e029ab1c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CP} \\perp \\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />. Then, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is isosceles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/0/a10459c41998a2ef73e2f7296c658de55c89ac8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is the perpindicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Then, reflect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/0/a10459c41998a2ef73e2f7296c658de55c89ac8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b4f897205beb16e266ea66d8ae8ece27cf5af8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M&#39;$\" width=\"23\" height=\"14\" />. This also maps <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f606484c4f15d045928e303e288937ac1dda0693.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A\\rightarrow B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/3/5839f374293c56c93f96697438431c3b767fe88d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CMB}\\cong\\angle{CM&#39;A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"153\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/108665435ad6cbe3bdc5aef6054a4a841fcc3386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CMA}=180-\\angle{ACM}-\\angle{MAC}=150^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"338\" height=\"16\" />. Further, since our reflection maps <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/0/7b07a23df5aa0a487fb6aa8362860ff5b95cd21b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A\\rightarrow A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/8/d38a8e094bb1278723f2a6e35279abbe82bcb4df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M\\rightarrow M&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/4/d243fcc2760ad620ef2a955ed2f5e763fdc2fc74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{M&#39;CB}=\\angle{ACM}=23^\\circ \\therefore \\angle{M&#39;CM}=60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"346\" height=\"16\" />. Since C is on the line of refelction, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/15405ccb27ae767617c90a51eb6b45f774004b21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CM\\cong CM&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" /> and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc49a378a926a18296ec3f92806979f9ee9db403.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{CMM&#39;}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" /> is equilateral. As such, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/9/de95b38f861b13cb934dcbe511007c5b4f365aa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{M&#39;MA}=150^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />. Then, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/8/698c721f20546ffbee73b0066e8ff382a597824c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{M&#39;AM}=\\theta, \\angle{AM&#39;M}=30-\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"258\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>By law of sines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/a/97a1f305613183b35e2afd4fdd13e155de54a4c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{CMA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/d/dbd2df77bb377e84a349d81252cd1e94acb95c1d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{MA}{\\sin(23)}=\\frac{CM}{\\sin(7)}\\implies MA = \\frac{CM\\sin(23)}{\\sin(7)}\\]\" width=\"331\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>By law of sines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/0/2601c3171f7f5ff0d191f0312d5ea5ef9db502f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AMM&#39;}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/0/510d9f45b9828814824259702699dc1e4f1054e8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{MA}{\\sin(30-\\theta)}=\\frac{MM&#39;}{\\sin(\\theta)}\\implies MA = \\frac{MM&#39;\\sin(30-\\theta)}{\\sin(\\theta)}\\]\" width=\"404\" height=\"43\" />\nSo:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/8/51823bf09dae0223e400e39ca6250e398a22b454.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{MM&#39;\\sin(30-\\theta)}{\\sin(\\theta)}=\\frac{CM\\sin(23)}{\\sin(7)}\\implies\\frac{\\sin(30-\\theta)}{\\sin(\\theta)}=\\frac{\\sin(23)}{\\sin(7)}\\because \\triangle{CMM&#39;} \\text{is equilateral}\\]\" width=\"666\" height=\"43\" />\nThis obviously gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/d/6ed485bad3091fbf973029f0c01dd0674790025a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = 7, 30-\\theta = 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/4/24472777e0d5d73384396551ba444a5f0c178127.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle{CMB}=\\angle{CM&#39;A}=\\angle{CM&#39;M}+\\angle{MM&#39;A}=60+23=\\boxed{083}\\]\" width=\"484\" height=\"23\" />\n~Stereotypicalmathnerd\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I\" title=\"2003 AIME I\">2003 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2003\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https